WEBVTT

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.700
June 4th. Cloudy.

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.070
21.5°. Southerly winds, blowing offshore.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.490
Face A, favorable.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.990
Clean conditions.

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.500
Hip high, with occasional waist high, waves.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.230
The size may increase 
depending on wind velocity.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.510
June 4th. Cloudy
 21.5° South winds
 Offshore. Face A, favorable
 Clean conditions
 Hip high, with occasional waist high, waves
 The size may increase 
depending on wind velocity.

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.510
Send

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.510
Done.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.260
Today's Shichirigahama...

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.950
Shirasu WAVE
 New Information Available

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:12.600
Okay!

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.090
<i>Every morning, Yuta updates a wave info app</i>

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:23.280
<i>that I check before heading to the beach.</i>

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:27.820
<i>This has become my daily routine.</i>

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.110
Tadao-san!

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.110
I'm off!

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:40.000
Yuta!

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:41.930
Morning!

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.620
Thanks for another update today!

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.850
Good morning!

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.870
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:44.740
Wave 7 A Heart Adrift Between the Waves

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.740
Good morning! Shirasu-don!

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.850
Oh! It's your favorite today, Yuta!

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.250
This will give me energy to start the day.

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.930
Then, without delay...

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:01.170
I'll have some!

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.500
What are you doing? That one's mine!

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.640
Won't you please let this cute 
underclassman of yours have it?

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.640
You should let your very 
cool upperclassman have it!

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:21.150
One shirasu-don contains, on average, 
732 shirasu, according to the data.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:22.500
Huh?

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.930
Which means...

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:29.330
we are receiving, on average, 
732 lives when we eat one.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.410
We must show our gratitude for these lives.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:32.970
Thank you for this food.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:41.150
<i>What he said is quite dignified, but...</i>

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:43.730
<i>I feel like maybe he just 
wanted to eat the biggest one...</i>

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.430
But still, Yuta, you're amazing.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:56.380
You update Shirasu Wave every 
morning without fail, right?

00:04:57.050 --> 00:05:00.060
In the beginning, it was 
just a sort of notebook...

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.050
I first started it to collect data.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:08.370
And now, all the surfers that come 
to Shonan to ride the waves check it.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:10.830
Thank you so much

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.200
You can't even sleep 
in peacefully at this rate, right?

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.960
It is, indeed, difficult 
to find a place to stop.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.340
Tadao-san! It was delicious. I owe you.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.720
No, just leave it.

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.710
Thank you.

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.260
Well, I'll see you at school.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.740
Yuta's acting weird.

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:35.740
How so?

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.980
You know how much Yuta loves shirasu. 
He has left one uneaten!

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.830
It's gotten pretty dark.

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.270
You're right.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:05.510
Hey, Yuta! Let's head home!

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:41.360
Is this Yuta?

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.670
He's adorable!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:46.350
Yeah.

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.010
Both his mama and papa are surfers.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:51.190
He was born into a family 
that runs a surf shop.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:53.960
You could say he was "born to be a surfer."

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.680
That's so cool!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:58.880
But the expectations 
of those around him are high,

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:01.440
so he's under a lot of pressure.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.160
When you've been doing it since you were a kid,

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:07.690
at a certain age, you start worrying 
that you're not making enough progress...

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:10.390
A slump, you mean?

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:52.230
<i>I made sure to be particular 
in choosing an appropriate wave.</i>

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:53.740
<i>My position wasn't bad, either.</i>

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:57.130
<i>According to the data, 
I should have been successful.</i>

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:00.230
<i>But...</i>

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:27.760
<i>Is this... my limit?</i>

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:38.780
Yay!

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.740
I've started to like heavy metal lately, too!

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.870
Hea-hea-hea-hea, vy-vy-vy-vy,
 me-me-me-me, tal!

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:53.300
Hea-hea-hea-hea, vy-vy-vy-vy, 
me-me-me-me, tal!

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:58.220
Hea-hea-hea-hea, vy-vy-vy-vy, 
me-me-me-me, tal!

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:11.840
Yuta!

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:16.320
Let's go get some yummy fried aji!

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:17.340
Okay?

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.490
According to my data...

00:09:26.210 --> 00:09:31.510
in this area, the likelihood of having 
a black kite steal your fried aji is 87 percent.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:33.960
We should probably take 
these home to eat them...

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:39.480
Stop! Give that back!

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:11.980
Yuta...

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.960
It's dangerous if you don't focus properly.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.070
You're really doing everything 
you can to interact with me.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.660
Why the sudden shift?

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:31.730
I'll just say it straight, then.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.540
Instead of worrying over things alone, 
I wish you'd talk to me.

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:40.740
It's not like I've been surfing since 
I was a kid, like you, Yuta, so...

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:44.520
I'm probably lacking 
as someone to talk to, but...

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.360
That's not true...

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.750
Sho didn't say anything to me.

00:11:04.660 --> 00:11:07.940
I don't want to regret anything 
the way I did back then.

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.140
So I wish you'd talk to me, about anything.

00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:15.170
We promised, didn't we? 
That we'd aim for the world...

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:35.410
If you're in a slump, then let's figure out 
how to get you out of it! Together!

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:37.310
Okay?

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:44.560
It isn't a slump.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:49.570
In the first place, that's a word that only 
those who have reached the top can use...

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:54.190
I'm grateful you feel that way.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.790
Thank you.

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:23.590
I see. So he's taking a break 
from school, too...

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:24.850
Yeah.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:29.450
Shirasu Wave is getting 
updated every day, but...

00:12:31.220 --> 00:12:33.790
His board must be lonely.

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:43.240
"If in doubt, paddle out."

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:55.370
<b><i>Enoshima Electric Railway</i></b>

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.550
<i>For people like me,</i>

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.390
<i>if we don't properly distance ourselves 
from the ocean at least once...</i>

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:12.390
<i>we won't be able to reset 
ourselves properly, either.</i>

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:21.900
<i>Tadao-san, I'm sorry...</i>

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:37.390
Ack! It's already this late?

00:13:37.390 --> 00:13:40.740
Huh? Where's the app 
notification? The update...

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.540
What?

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:44.920
An Apology

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.920
New message

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.930
I won't be able to keep 
my promise. I'm sorry.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:51.150
He...

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:55.400
Is he planning to quit surfing?

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.290
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:10.450
<i>Yuta's going to quit surfing!</i>

00:14:10.750 --> 00:14:11.700
Maybe.

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:15.620
Last night, he said something about looking 
for a path other than surfing.

00:14:16.410 --> 00:14:19.080
I have to go see him.

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.810
Yuta's in the mountains. 
He's at his grandma's house.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.060
Wait a minute.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:31.060
Dang it! What can I do? How can I...

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.810
<i>That face...</i>

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:50.110
<i>All he needs to do is have 
fun surfing, like that, but...</i>

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.170
<i>Lately, Yuta's expression 
has only been troubled.</i>

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:05.510
The address is somewhere around here!

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:07.560
So, which way should I go?

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:10.750
<i>That's right. I have some really good data!</i>

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.140
Yuta! Watch this

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.140
Yuta! Watch this 100 times

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.140
Beautiful Riding Technique Compilation

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:17.640
Hey.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:20.980
This is Yuta's grandma's address.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.650
And take this with you, too.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:40.580
Yuta! Watch this 100 times

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:40.580
Beautiful Riding Technique
Compilation

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:41.710
Honestly.

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:44.210
I don't understand what Masaki 
is trying to tell me.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:49.410
I've already watched this video dozens of times 
and finished a thorough study of it.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:57.570
It really is magnificent.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.510
Such perfect form.

00:16:14.070 --> 00:16:15.220
Surprise!

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.890
Why send me a video of Sho?

00:16:26.510 --> 00:16:28.280
We're talking about you here, Yuta.

00:16:28.280 --> 00:16:31.520
You've got it all in your 
head as data already, right?

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:33.010
Of course.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:38.350
Sho's positioning, what waves he chose... 
I've already analyzed all of it.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.330
No.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.610
There's something you haven't analyzed.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:46.590
What would that be?

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:49.520
Sho's face!

00:16:49.520 --> 00:16:50.950
H-His face?

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:55.070
Um... Why would I analyze his handsomeness?

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:59.600
If I were to do that, I'd have to go back 
15 generations, to the Warring States era,

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:02.930
and find data on his 
ancestors' faces, or else...

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:05.070
Well, we are talking about Sho's ancestors.

00:17:05.070 --> 00:17:07.090
I'm sure they were handsome Warring
States military commanders—

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.560
That's not what I'm talking about!

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:11.800
I'm talking about how Sho 
is having fun riding the waves!

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:19.430
His face says he's having so 
much fun, he can't get enough.

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:28.440
You haven't analyzed 
Sho's face there, have you?

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:32.650
It's true.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:38.300
Sho's face there... the way it shines, 
I haven't looked at that as data.

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:49.800
Imagine me missing such an important factor.

00:17:51.030 --> 00:17:54.450
Not physical, but emotional...

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.210
Joy enters the bloodstream...

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.970
and rushes through the whole body, 
resulting in new potential worth...

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.110
1,173 points.

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:07.730
So...

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.570
It's been a while. What do you think?

00:18:09.570 --> 00:18:11.730
Is that— Where did you...

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:16.240
Apparently, your parents 
entrusted it to Tadao-san.

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:31.820
You really treasured it, didn't you?

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:33.860
Of course.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:38.260
It was the first board 
I'd ever had that was all mine.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:41.760
I was so happy. I didn't want to 
let it go for even one second.

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:50.960
Yuta, let's go!

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:52.770
The same wave will never come again!

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:56.530
While we're sitting here, 
our waves will disappear!

00:18:57.370 --> 00:18:59.710
Our waves, huh?

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:13.410
<i>I couldn't pick the right waves...</i>

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:15.550
<i>and I didn't know the names 
of any of the maneuvers.</i>

00:19:15.990 --> 00:19:19.550
<i>I just faced every wave as it came.</i>

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:27.060
<i>I learned the feel of the waves 
with my body, not my head.</i>

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:31.560
<i>That's right. This is how 
amazing waves can feel!</i>

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.330
I'm happy for him.

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:43.820
Now, we're going in, too!

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:44.870
Yeah!

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:56.190
To be honest, I was jealous.

00:19:57.080 --> 00:20:01.170
Of Sho, of course, but also 
of Kosuke-san and Masaki, too.

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.960
What? Of me, too?

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.940
But today I understood.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:10.080
The emotions with which you 
face the waves are important data,

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:11.850
even beyond skill improvement.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:13.740
Yes.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.420
Thank you.

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:18.040
I'll be counting on you in the future, too.

00:20:24.360 --> 00:20:26.240
Welcome back, Shirasu Wave-san!!

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.370
Welcome back. 
Infinite gratitude.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:31.840
I only just restarted the app.

00:20:31.840 --> 00:20:34.570
You must be connected through the ocean.

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:45.220
<i>There's only one ocean.</i>

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:52.400
<i>The feelings of all of us surfers... 
I know they're reaching Sho, too.</i>

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:58.150
This arrived with a thud 
from your family, Masaki.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.150
Dried Sweet Potato

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.540
Dried sweet potato!

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:02.960
I'm having some now!

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:05.660
This is an amazing amount...

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:13.590
Bill?

00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:16.420
Hey, everyone. It's been a while.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.690
I happened to be in the 
area, so I dropped by.

00:21:19.690 --> 00:21:22.420
The thing is, we finished a new poster.

00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.600
For the Forest Cup, right?

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:33.700
It will be held in Chiba, 
like the 2020 world competition.

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:36.190
Bill, you're entering, right?

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:38.440
Of course.

00:21:42.970 --> 00:21:43.940
Looking forward to it.

00:21:45.370 --> 00:21:47.440
Fuke-san is gonna be in it, too?

00:21:47.440 --> 00:21:52.450
Fuke? You mean... the one 
called Miyazaki's bucking bronco?

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:53.460
Yes.

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:57.900
He's always aiming for unprecedented 
achievements... He's very meritocratic.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:22:01.090
the solitary genius, Fuke Rindo.

00:22:01.090 --> 00:22:03.210
Someone that famous is competing, too?

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:06.240
We're gonna beat him!

00:22:06.780 --> 00:22:07.670
Yeah!

00:22:08.590 --> 00:22:09.540
Yes!

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:53.990
Wave 8   My Guardian Spirit
